[2026-10-31] rc:4433207342 inline on src/test/fuzz/p2p_transport_serialization.cpp by uqlidi (edited 2026-10-31):
I think the transport never rekeys here. The loop stops at 100 actions, so a stream holds fewer than 100 packets, and the transport rekeys every 224:
https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/a773e1e33b349dc819b5a0edc1c7a4839dc73b48/src/bip324.h#L26

Maybe add an action that appends a run of empty decoys? With the diff below, libFuzzer's coverage report shows this rekey branch hit:
https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/blob/a773e1e33b349dc819b5a0edc1c7a4839dc73b48/src/crypto/chacha20poly1305.cpp#L106-L108

```diff
diff --git a/src/test/fuzz/p2p_transport_serialization.cpp b/src/test/fuzz/p2p_transport_serialization.cpp
index 852994afe..c823f669d 100644
--- a/src/test/fuzz/p2p_transport_serialization.cpp
+++ b/src/test/fuzz/p2p_transport_serialization.cpp
@@ -474,6 +474,16 @@ FUZZ_TARGET(p2p_transport_v2_receive, .init = initialize_p2p_transport_serializa
                 peer.Encrypt(contents, MakeByteSpan(aad), ignore, MakeWritableByteSpan(stream).subspan(start));
                 aad.clear();
                 if (corrupt) flip_fn(start);
+            },
+            // A run of empty decoys, so the transport has to rekey (every REKEY_INTERVAL packets).
+            [&] {
+                const auto count{provider.ConsumeIntegralInRange<unsigned>(1, BIP324Cipher::REKEY_INTERVAL)};
+                for (unsigned i{0}; i < count; ++i) {
+                    const auto start = stream.size();
+                    stream.resize(start + BIP324Cipher::EXPANSION);
+                    peer.Encrypt({}, MakeByteSpan(aad), /*ignore=*/true, MakeWritableByteSpan(stream).subspan(start));
+                    aad.clear();
+                }
             }
         );
     }
```
